 "1-10": {
  "first": "flagged: The reading leaves out the main point of the verse, which is the actual comparison of the armies' sizes or strengths.",
  "second": "flagged: The reading adds that Sanjaya is speaking to the king, which neither translation mentions.",
  "redraft": "Sanjaya tells the king that their army is defended by Bhishma, and the other army is defended by Bhima. He compares them, saying one army seems limited while the other appears much greater.",
  "translations_disagree": "Besant reads the prince's own army as insufficient and the other as sufficient; Swarupananda reads his own as impossible to count and the other as easy to number. A plain reading would have to choose between them, so this verse has none until a reviewer decides."
 },
